Horn Nature is an organization working to protect the environment and improve the lives of communities through practical and community-focused initiatives. Its work covers important areas such as environmental conservation, climate change, biodiversity protection, land and water management, community empowerment, and livelihood development.
Horn Nature recognizes that environmental challenges can directly affect communities and their livelihoods. Issues such as climate change, water scarcity, land degradation, loss of biodiversity, and limited access to natural resources can create significant challenges for local populations. Through its programs, Horn Nature aims to address these challenges while supporting communities in finding practical solutions.
The organization also focuses on community empowerment by encouraging local participation and creating opportunities for people to take an active role in development activities. Women, youth, farmers, pastoralists, and other community members can benefit from initiatives designed to strengthen knowledge, skills, resources, and local capacity.
